---Message describing Transport object.
---@class gcp.networkconnectivity_v1.Transport
---@field mtuLimit? number Output only. The maximum transmission unit (MTU) of a packet that can be sent over this transport.
---@field remoteProfile? string Optional. Immutable. Name of the remoteTransportProfile that this Transport is connecting to.
---@field bandwidth? gcp.networkconnectivity_v1.TransportBandwidthEnum Optional. Bandwidth of the Transport. This must be one of the supported bandwidths for the remote profile, and must be set when no activation key is being provided.
---@field remoteAccountId? string Optional. Immutable. The user supplied account id for the CSP associated with the remote profile.
---@field autoAccept? boolean Optional. Immutable. Controls whether resources proposed by the Transport are automatically accepted on behalf of the user. List of actions that can be automatically accepted are: 1. VPC Peering creation 2. Routing VPC Spoke creation 3. Hybrid Spoke creation
---@field network? string Optional. Immutable. Resource URI of the Network that will be peered with this Transport. This field must be provided during resource creation and cannot be changed.
---@field createTime? string Output only. Create time stamp.
---@field labels? gcp.networkconnectivity_v1.StringMap Optional. Labels as key value pairs.
---@field peeringNetwork? string Output only. VPC Network URI that was created for the VPC Peering connection to the provided `network`. If VPC Peering is disconnected, this can be used to re-establish.
---@field state? gcp.networkconnectivity_v1.TransportStateEnum Output only. State of the underlying connectivity.
---@field advertisedRoutes? gcp.networkconnectivity_v1.StringList Optional. List of IP Prefixes that will be advertised to the remote provider. Both IPv4 and IPv6 addresses are supported.
---@field description? string Optional. Description of the Transport.
---@field name? string Identifier. Name of the resource.
---@field stackType? gcp.networkconnectivity_v1.TransportStackTypeEnum Optional. IP version stack for the established connectivity.
---@field hub? string Optional. Immutable. The NCC Hub that the Transport should attach to. The hub must be in the same project as the Transport. Format: `{hub}` or `projects/{project}/locations/global/hubs/{hub}`
---@field updateTime? string Output only. Update time stamp.
---@field providedActivationKey? string Optional. Immutable. Key used for establishing a connection with the remote transport. This key can only be provided if the profile supports an INPUT key flow and the resource is in the PENDING_KEY state.
---@field generatedActivationKey? string Output only. Google-generated activation key. This is only output if the selected profile supports an OUTPUT key flow. Inputting this to the provider is only valid while the resource is in a PENDING_KEY state. Once the provider has accepted the key, the resource will move to the CONFIGURING state.
---@field pscRoutingEnabled? boolean Optional. Immutable. Controls whether a Routing VPC Spoke should be created and attached to the NCC Hub. This will provide Private Service Connect (PSC) connectivity through NCC. This can only be set when the Transport is first created.

---@alias gcp.networkconnectivity_v1.TransportBandwidthEnum "BANDWIDTH_UNSPECIFIED"|"BPS_50M"|"BPS_100M"|"BPS_200M"|"BPS_300M"|"BPS_400M"|"BPS_500M"|"BPS_1G"|"BPS_2G"|"BPS_5G"|"BPS_10G"|"BPS_20G"|"BPS_50G"|"BPS_100G"

